  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The title is a quote by 17th century Swiss mathematician, Jakob Bernoulli. The images, diagrams and equations reference the inherent nature of fractal geometry through the continual appearance of the logarithmic spiral."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This book is a limited edition, hand-bound artists' book by Susan Lowdermilk. Imagery by the artist was created by using lithography, collagraph, woodcut and powdered pigment on Stonehenge and Somerset papers."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="563" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Bound in black cloth over board, in a three-panel wrap-around cover. Titles and colophon on labels pasted onto the front and back covers, respectively. Endpapers covered with mathematical diagrams and equations, silver-gray on black paper. Opens to reveal a tunnel book in the central panel.</subfield>
